course: dictionary
lesson: 2901
title: A word with a title
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dowager is a widow who keeps a title or property from her dead husband. It is a noun, so it names a person, and the word often sits in a title like «dowager duchess».
explain: Context clues help you. «Empress Dowager Cixi was the most powerful person at the Qing court» tells you Cixi held the title of empress, and dowager means she was an empress who was a widow.
explain: In stories, dowager can also mean a grand, dignified old lady. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: A dowager is a widow with a title or property from her dead husband.
fact: «Dowager duchess» and «Queen Dowager» are examples of this title.
fact: Informally, «dowager» can mean a grand, dignified old lady.
fact: «Empress Dowager Cixi» was the most powerful person at the Qing court from 1861 to 1908.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: In «Empress Dowager Cixi was the most powerful person at the Qing court», what is a dowager? | A young princess who has not yet married | *A widow with a title from her dead husband | A captain of a ship | A servant who cleans the palace
exercise: Which phrase matches the informal meaning of dowager? | A young girl who runs fast | A rainy day in Scotland | A small boat on a lake | *A grand, dignified old lady
exercise: In «Queen Dowager», what does dowager tell us about the queen? | She is very young and new to the palace | *She is a widow who keeps her title from her husband | She lives beside the sea | Her husband, the king, has died and she keeps her title
test: In «the Queen Dowager ruled from the palace», what does dowager mean? | *A widow with a title from her dead husband | A dog that guards the palace | A mountain near the sea | A kind of jewel
test: Which best describes a dowager in a classic novel? | A tiny fish that lives in rivers | A brand of tea sold in shops | A young soldier who fights in a war | *A noble widow, often the mother of the new duke or king
exam: Which meaning fits dowager best? | A ruler who has never married | A boat that sails on a river | *A widow with a title from her dead husband | A soldier in a civil war
